{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And you shall warn them.</b> The second path that I mentioned: you are obligated to teach them and instruct them in matters of doubt, for it is a great burden to make known every deed that they shall do. The sense of והזהרת is from ולא נזהר (Ezekiel 33:5), and its meaning is 'to be guarded.'" "<b>אתהם.</b> Two words." "And it is to warn them concerning positive commandments, and concerning negative commandments bound to the heart, which is the essence — such as to love HaShem and to cleave to Him, and to fear Him, and to walk after Him, and to circumcise the foreskin of the heart, and not to hate one's brother, and not to bear a grudge and not to take vengeance, and likewise Moses said: in your mouth and in your heart, to do it (Deuteronomy 30:14), and many like these." "<b>They shall walk in it.</b> Like אשר ילכו בה." "<b>And the deed that they shall do.</b> These are positive commandments for action, and most of them are not positive commandments that stand on their own, but are for remembrance — such as the Sabbath and the festivals and redemption of the son and love of the convert and tzitzit and tefillin and prayer and mezuzah, also shaatnez, and many others; in their places I shall explain them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:42.531225271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}